{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SESSION CLOSE. Epic 061c: 37 of 38 descendants closed. eb6e (the production Bedrock cutover) CLOSED with all 15 criteria evidenced. 8625 open with its ADR merged. Two NEW blockers on the epic, both filed and one implemented.\n\nDELIVERED\n* eb6e CLOSED. Production review bot runs on Bedrock: three class slots verified in-container, provenance provider=bedrock on a real Gerrit vote (change 1329), per-call usage log 8/8 on bedrock: profiles with ZERO direct-Anthropic, frontier->opus and standard->sonnet observed in production, nonzero cache_read. Bedrock InvokeModel client-error alarm declared, APPLIED, and observed moving INSUFFICIENT_DATA->OK on real data; ARN and a delivered forced notification recorded. Induced VOTER_ERROR drill on the pre-cutover Anthropic path with an observed OK->ALARM transition. Denied-access drill (explicit IAM Deny, budget narrowed to 1 with operator approval) producing VOTER_ERROR, a fail-closed -1 and no approving vote, then a clean retry after restore. Kill switch executed end-to-end with a real Anthropic-path vote and the cutover re-applied.\n* d2ce CLOSED. rebar.toml now sets [llm] model AND [llm.model_classes] to the three bedrock profiles. Local Bedrock use CONFIRMED BY A REAL GATE: review-plan completed PASS with 5/5 calls on bedrock: and zero direct-Anthropic, all three classes exercised.\n* 4e71 CLOSED. bedrock_model.py no longer tells operators to set AWS_REGION, which does not resolve a region (measured on botocore 1.43.62 with AWS_DEFAULT_REGION genuinely unset).\n* 8625's ADR MERGED as d416ab9846 (ADR 0059, +992 lines, plus 132 lines of llm-framework.md).\n* Cleared a red main nobody had noticed: 34cd landed a CloudWatch alarm that was never applied. Applied it; drift clean.\n\nTHE BIGGEST CORRECTION: eb6e's CERTIFIED plan contained a FALSE SHOWSTOPPER that had already forced a BLOCK and two amendments. It claimed the review-bot image lacked pydantic_ai.providers.bedrock so the class-slot flip alone would stop the gate voting. Measured in the running container, image built from current main: the exact import SUCCEEDS. The bedrock extra contributes only boto3, which the reviewbot extra already installs at the same version; the module ships in the base wheel. Three independent plan-review criteria (E4, G6, T3) later reached the same conclusion at critical severity. The reasoning error, worth naming: absence of the EXTRA was taken to imply absence of the MODULE, and confirmed by READING packaging rather than EXECUTING the import - including by me, who wrote \"verified against the tree\".\n\nNEW BLOCKERS ON THE EPIC (both linked blocks -> 061c)\n* 129e - the cutover SILENTLY removed server-side web search from BLOCKING criterion T1, gated by resolved.startswith(\"anthropic\"). Operator ruled web access is required regardless of provider. MEASURED: Bedrock cannot carry the native tool (UserError, Supported: []), but pydantic-ai's WebSearch(native=..., local='duckduckgo') is native-or-local in one object, so no homegrown fetch tool is needed. Change 1344 implements it but is blocked -1/-1; see the ticket, the block is cheap to clear.\n* (8625 remains open; its AC2 requires EXECUTING every runnable command in llm-framework.md's provider section - not satisfiable by inspection.)\n\nFILED OUTSIDE THE EPIC\n* e4f4 (P1) - a shell-expanded comment body wrote LIVE CREDENTIALS into the ticket store. My quoting error: a body quoting upstream text containing backticked `local` was passed inside double quotes, so zsh command-substituted it and its builtin dumped the whole environment - an Anthropic key, TWO GitHub PATs, an OpenAI-style key. NOTHING REACHED A REMOTE: GitHub secret-scanning push protection blocked it and the commit is on no remote branch. Exactly one commit/one file affected out of 108 unpushed. The only control that stopped it was outside the project. It also wedged 108 legitimate commits behind it, so the store's evidence is currently local-only.\n* 1dbe (P1) - prompt cache is WRITTEN on every gate call and NEVER READ across calls. Two back-to-back reviews of different tickets inside the TTL: run B wrote again (2800->2908, 1545->1608, 4871->4934) with reads 0. Write sizes track input deltas, so the marked prefix VARIES PER TICKET and the key is never reusable. Intra-call reuse works (production 9-step records read 386k), so the read path is fine - the prefix is not stable. Costs premium-rate write tokens on every review for zero benefit.\n* 61d8, 1c39, 9baf, 66af filed earlier from eb6e's work (botocore retry gap; terraform drift never gating a Gerrit change; the voter_errors alarm notifying nobody - 2 of 12 alarms silent; the review bot logging its webhook token in plaintext).\n\nMISTAKES I MADE, recorded because the patterns repeat\n* Twice restored a mutated file with git checkout -- while my own edit was UNCOMMITTED, silently reverting my work and confounding three mutation results each time. The tell was the restored baseline not returning to green. A mutation experiment is only valid if the restore returns to the state you believe it does.\n* Read exit codes through pipes (| head, PIPESTATUS in the wrong shell) and got the pipe's status instead of the gate's.\n* Concluded \"the web-search branch is dormant\" TWICE from narrow searches - I checked only the .rebar overlay and missed the PACKAGED criteria_routing.json, then grepped web= in two files and missed runner.py's call site. The operator corrected me both times. Search all file types across src/ before concluding an absence.\n* Nearly filed a bogus \"stuck in_flight counter\" bug: I read in_flight=2 with 0.13% CPU and no LLM_TOKEN_USAGE hits as a leak. Recent activity logs as \"llm call [...]\", and an agentic review is I/O-bound so low CPU is expected. The bot was healthy.\n* Called in_flight_reviews() via docker compose exec and got 0 while /health said 2, nearly reading that as /health lying. exec starts a FRESH process with its own module state; only /health, served by the server process, is a valid reading. Same class as reading an env var on the HOST and attributing it to the container, which I also did.\n* Left an IAM Deny in place longer than intended because the removal command sat behind the same long-running observation command. The operator asked \"is the deny there now?\" and it was. A fault injection's revert must never share a command with its observation.\n\nDURABLE FACTS THE NEXT SESSION SHOULD NOT REDISCOVER\n* THERE ARE EIGHT CI-ONLY GATE SCRIPTS and NONE is in make lint: check_comment_hygiene, check_config_reads, check_docs_index, check_raw_git_writes, check_readme_quickstart, check_server_manifest, check_verify_gate_parity, check_wall_clock_asserts. The inherited checklist named two, which is what earned a Verified -1. The authoritative list is .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml, not the Makefile and not prose.\n* A Verified -1 whose failing step is a GATE SCRIPT should be checked for the script's EXISTENCE in the tree before its output is read as a violation. Gerrit CI runs the TARGET branch's workflow against the patchset's tree, so a gate added to main after your base fails on a missing file. Rebase, do not debug.\n* POST /a/changes/N/submit with no body returns HTTP 400 \"Expected JSON object\" - which reads like a permissions problem. Send -d '{}'.\n* rebar list accepts NEITHER --limit NOR -o json, and passing them yields EMPTY OUTPUT rather than an error, which reads as \"nothing exists\".\n* Bugs and session_logs are EXEMPT from the plan-review CLAIM gate per rebar.toml - but a LARGE bugfix still needs a certified attestation to pass the Gerrit bugfix-size gate (>150 non-test lines). That is what blocks 1344.\n* review-plan can return PASS and exit 11 when signing hits an flock. sign-review re-signs from the recorded sidecar with NO LLM spend - always try it before paying again.\n* NEVER pass untrusted or quoted text directly inside double quotes to rebar comment. Write it to a file and pass \"$(cat file)\" - the substitution result is not re-scanned. This is what caused e4f4."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785818358775052001,"uuid":"82f5c0b6-8b15-4f0e-b7c3-48c48574aa4b"}